      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": ["# RIFE video interpolation (WAN-method branch)\n\n1. Upload the finished source video in **Load Video**.\n2. RIFE 4.7 uses GPU neural interpolation; it is not the basic optical-flow method.\n3. For a 24 fps source to a 60 fps master: set multiplier to **5** and Create Video FPS to **120**. This preserves duration. Then decimate the 120 fps master to 60 fps (every second frame) while retaining original audio.\n4. Upscale only after interpolation.\n\nRecommended RIFE controls: `rife47.pth`, multiplier `5`, `float16`, fast mode enabled, ensemble enabled. Lower scale factor only if VRAM is tight."]
    },
